Package: shinobi-desktop
Version: 0.1.0
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Shinobi OS Maintainers <maintainers@shinobi-os.local>
Depends: shinobi-core (= 0.1.0), dbus-user-session, hyprland, quickshell, wofi, mako-notifier, swaybg, hypridle, hyprlock, hyprpolkitagent, kitty, sddm, plymouth, pipewire, wireplumber, pipewire-pulse, network-manager, bluez, xdg-desktop-portal, xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland, xdg-desktop-portal-gtk, grim, slurp, wl-clipboard, cliphist, libnotify-bin, jq, btop, rsync, fontconfig
Description: Shinobi OS desktop layer
 The Hyprland desktop Shinobi OS presents: dotfiles for Hyprland, Quickshell,
 wofi and kitty, the Plymouth boot splash, the wallpaper, and the portal
 configuration.
 .
 The desktop stack is declared here rather than in a list unique to the live
 image, so an installed system and the image it was installed from cannot
 drift apart. It used to live in the ISO's package list alone, which meant
 installing to disk produced Kali's own desktop with none of this -- the layer
 existed only as a side effect of how the image was built. One declaration now
 feeds both paths.
 .
 shinobi-setup applies the dotfiles to an account; nothing here edits a home
 directory. See shinobi-setup(8).